There are many different reasons why people decide to be vegetarian, from health concerns, to animal welfare, to environmental reasoning. In this article, we will discuss some of the most common reasons people become vegetarian. 

The health reasons that people choose to become vegetarian include the following:

- Lower risk of heart disease; 
- Lower rates of obesity; 
- Lower overall cancer rates; 
- Lower rates of diabetes; 
- Lower cholesterol levels; 
- Lower blood pressure levels, and 
- More energy levels. 

Consuming more whole grains, fruits and vegetables, and legumes instead of animal products can be beneficial to your health. 

Animal welfare is another reason why people choose to stop eating meat. This reason focuses on the treatment of the animals that are used for meat production. Some people choose to stop eating meat based on the ethics of eating animals that are bred in unsanitary conditions, or are given drugs, or are slaughtered inhumanely. 

The last reason that people usually choose to stop eating meat is for environmental reasons. This can include everything from the impact of raising animals on the environment, to the environmental impact of transporting the meat.
